WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
ShabadVerse
Explore connections across Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji for a khoj or a parkaran.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.800
Find a shabad from words you remember.

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.900
Type first letters, ਤ ਠ ਤ ਪ ਅ,
to find this verse on Ang 268.

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.700
Tap ✨ and type a line in English letters.

5
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.900
MATCHED LINE marks a verse that holds
the words you typed.

6
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:26.950
Type a Gurmukhi word, and MATCHED WORDS
marks the verses that use it.

7
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.700
Or start from a theme. Open Topics
and choose Haumai.

8
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:36.300
The list starts with its 73 strongest matches,
where Haumai carries the most weight.

9
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.800
Open one.

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.500
Whole-shabad matching links shabads that
share concepts and meaning.

11
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.350
The connections group under concept names.

12
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.050
Switch Match to A line.

13
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:53.000
Line matching compares verse translations.

14
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.750
Tap the shabad, then VERSES, to match
from another verse.

15
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.100
The connections change.

16
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.150
They group under a Gurmukhi word both verses
share, or under Similar translation.

17
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.200
SELECTIVE sets how closely
shabads must match.

18
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.300
Raise it to keep only
the closest connections.

19
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.750
Lower it to see more distant ones.

20
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.450
SPREAD only spaces the graph out.

21
00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:21.533
Switch back to Whole shabad
and start a set.

22
00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:24.333
Tap a connection to add it or explore it.

23
00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:26.783
Explore opens its own connections.

24
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:30.833
Then tap the next,
add it, and explore again.

25
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:34.583
The trail above the graph keeps your path.

26
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:38.433
Each step builds a journey for a khoj
or a parkaran.

27
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.883
Review shows the set in full, in order.

28
00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:46.383
Connections are suggestions. Read each shabad
in full before you choose.

29
00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:49.083
Share copies a link that keeps the order.

30
00:01:49.183 --> 00:01:53.733
A fresh browser opens the same set.

31
00:01:53.850 --> 00:02:02.850
Try a line you know well.
shabadverse.com
Tell us where a connection holds, and where it fails.
Report an example: github.com/ujjaldidarsingh/ShabadVerse/issues
